            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A mutable function default can retain state between calls."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Mutable default argument** (`PY-COR-001`)\n\nA mutable function default can retain state between calls.\n\n**Remediation:** Use None as the default and create a new value inside the function.\n\n**Not reported when:**\n\n- The default is an immutable literal (None, numbers, strings, tuples) or a call to anything other than list/dict/set/bytearray; list, dict and set displays, their comprehensions, and those four factory calls are what is flagged (python_rules._MUTABLE_LITERALS / _MUTABLE_FACTORIES).\n- The parameter is intentionally a shared, documented cache or sentinel: the rule cannot see intent, so confirm before rewriting.\n\n[PY-COR-001 in the rule reference](https://github.com/AmitSinghOM/code-quality-analyzer/blob/v3.5.0/docs/RULES.md#py-cor-001-mutable-default-argument)",
                "text": "Use None as the default and create a new value inside the function."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/AmitSinghOM/code-quality-analyzer/blob/v3.5.0/docs/RULES.md#py-cor-001-mutable-default-argument",
              "id": "PY-COR-001",
              "name": "mutable-default-argument",
              "properties": {
                "category": "correctness",
                "confidence": "high",
                "defaultSeverity": "warning",
                "language": "python"
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Mutable default argument"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A broad exception handler can hide failures it cannot recover from."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Broad exception handler** (`PY-COR-002`)\n\nA broad exception handler can hide failures it cannot recover from.\n\n**Remediation:** Catch the narrow exception types the operation can recover from.\n\n**Not reported when:**\n\n- The handler catches a specific exception class rather than Exception or BaseException.\n- The handler body is only `pass`/`...` (a bare `except:`, `except Exception: pass`, ...): PY-COR-003 reports the swallow and one handler yields one finding, not two.\n- The handler ends with a bare `raise` or `raise <bound name>` (no `from`): `except BaseException: cleanup(); raise` is a `finally` with access to the exception and the only way to guarantee cleanup on KeyboardInterrupt; ruff BLE001 exempts the same shape. Logging without re-raising, or wrapping in a new exception type, is still reported.\n\n[PY-COR-002 in the rule reference](https://github.com/AmitSinghOM/code-quality-analyzer/blob/v3.5.0/docs/RULES.md#py-cor-002-broad-exception-handler)",
                "text": "Catch the narrow exception types the operation can recover from."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/AmitSinghOM/code-quality-analyzer/blob/v3.5.0/docs/RULES.md#py-cor-002-broad-exception-handler",
              "id": "PY-COR-002",
              "name": "broad-exception-handler",
              "properties": {
                "category": "correctness",
                "confidence": "high",
                "defaultSeverity": "warning",
                "language": "python"
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Broad exception handler"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A locally acquired resource is not protected by structural cleanup."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Resource without guaranteed cleanup** (`PY-COR-006`)\n\nA locally acquired resource is not protected by structural cleanup.\n\n**Remediation:** Use a context manager or guarantee cleanup with try/finally.\n\n**Not reported when:**\n\n- The resource is opened inside a `with` statement or returned to a caller that manages its lifetime.\n- The call is not in the fixed resource-call allowlist (python_resources._RESOURCE_CALLS).\n- Cleanup is guaranteed by an enclosing try/finally.\n\n[PY-COR-006 in the rule reference](https://github.com/AmitSinghOM/code-quality-analyzer/blob/v3.5.0/docs/RULES.md#py-cor-006-resource-without-guaranteed-cleanup)",
                "text": "Use a context manager or guarantee cleanup with try/finally."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/AmitSinghOM/code-quality-analyzer/blob/v3.5.0/docs/RULES.md#py-cor-006-resource-without-guaranteed-cleanup",
              "id": "PY-COR-006",
              "name": "resource-without-guaranteed-cleanup",
              "properties": {
                "category": "correctness",
                "confidence": "high",
                "defaultSeverity": "warning",
                "language": "python"
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Resource without guaranteed cleanup"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A function declares more effective parameters than the supported limit."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Excessive parameters** (`PY-MAINT-004`)\n\nA function declares more effective parameters than the supported limit.\n\n**Remediation:** Group related inputs in a cohesive value object or split the responsibility.\n\n**Not reported when:**\n\n- The parameter count is at or below the configured limit; `self`/`cls` are not counted.\n\n[PY-MAINT-004 in the rule reference](https://github.com/AmitSinghOM/code-quality-analyzer/blob/v3.5.0/docs/RULES.md#py-maint-004-excessive-parameters)",
                "text": "Group related inputs in a cohesive value object or split the responsibility."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/AmitSinghOM/code-quality-analyzer/blob/v3.5.0/docs/RULES.md#py-maint-004-excessive-parameters",
              "id": "PY-MAINT-004",
              "name": "excessive-parameters",
              "properties": {
                "category": "maintainability",
                "confidence": "high",
                "defaultSeverity": "warning",
                "language": "python"
              },
              "shortDescription": {
