            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "subprocess.*(cmd, shell=True), os.system(cmd) or os.popen(cmd) with a non-literal command lets a shell re-parse runtime data."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Shell command assembled at runtime** (`PY-SEC-002`)\n\nsubprocess.*(cmd, shell=True), os.system(cmd) or os.popen(cmd) with a non-literal command lets a shell re-parse runtime data.\n\n**CWE:** CWE-78\n\n**Remediation:** Pass an argument list without shell=True; quote with shlex.quote if a shell is unavoidable.\n\n**Not reported when:**\n\n- The command is a string literal, or the subprocess call has no shell=True keyword (a list of arguments is never reported).\n- os.system/os.popen are only recognised through the `os.` qualifier; a `from os import system` call is not seen.\n\n[PY-SEC-002 in the rule reference](https://github.com/AmitSinghOM/code-quality-analyzer/blob/v3.5.0/docs/RULES.md#py-sec-002-shell-command-assembled-at-runtime)",
                "text": "Pass an argument list without shell=True; quote with shlex.quote if a shell is unavoidable."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/AmitSinghOM/code-quality-analyzer/blob/v3.5.0/docs/RULES.md#py-sec-002-shell-command-assembled-at-runtime",
              "id": "PY-SEC-002",
              "name": "shell-command-from-runtime-string",
              "properties": {
