              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "eval() or exec() receives a value that is not a string literal."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**eval/exec of a runtime string** (`PY-SEC-003`)\n\neval() or exec() receives a value that is not a string literal.\n\n**CWE:** CWE-95\n\n**Remediation:** Use ast.literal_eval for data, a dispatch table for behaviour, or importlib for module names.\n\n**Not reported when:**\n\n- The first argument is a string literal, or the callee is an attribute (pandas `df.eval`, `ast.literal_eval`) rather than the bare builtin.\n\n[PY-SEC-003 in the rule reference](https://github.com/AmitSinghOM/code-quality-analyzer/blob/v3.5.0/docs/RULES.md#py-sec-003-evalexec-of-a-runtime-string)",
                "text": "Use ast.literal_eval for data, a dispatch table for behaviour, or importlib for module names."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/AmitSinghOM/code-quality-analyzer/blob/v3.5.0/docs/RULES.md#py-sec-003-evalexec-of-a-runtime-string",
              "id": "PY-SEC-003",
